name issue_76_tcc_v2_high_jitter
describe 40 ms jitter with reordering, transport-cc feedback as libwebrtc's generator (#76 group 1)
# libwebrtc's TransportSequenceNumberFeedbackGenenerator keeps arrivals 500 ms and reports a packet that
# arrives behind a sent report again, so the delay-based estimator sees the reordered packets in order.
# Seeds 1-5: video delay p95 159-253 ms with `tcc v1`'s 1547 ms; libwebrtc (CI compare-webrtc, high_jitter): 136 ms.
# Target (#76 / parity): within the parity band of libwebrtc's 136 ms; video bitrate (libwebrtc 584 kbps) needs #19.
tcc v2
duration 30s
at 0s capacity=3000kbps delay=30ms jitter=40ms reorder=on queue=300ms
# Flip (#61, needs-human): was `video.e2e_delay_p95_ms < 300`; seeds 1-5 with every v2 switch on: 191-1623 ms; libwebrtc 136 ms (10 seeds). Worse than libwebrtc; owned by #24 (video jitter estimate and render timing).
# Target: the original line, once the item that owns the gap lands.
expect video.e2e_delay_p95_ms < 1700
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 500
expect audio.interruptions == 0
expect audio.concealed_pct < 2
